        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(worktrees): configurable cleanup limits (max count, max total size) with Settings UI",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nManaged worktrees accumulate without any disk bound: hourly cleanup only removes session/Workboard worktrees idle for more than 7 days, so busy hosts can hold dozens of multi-GB checkouts with no way to cap count or total size. Closes #106213.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOperators need Cursor-style cleanup tunables (\"Max worktrees\", \"Max total size (GB)\") so managed-worktree disk usage stays bounded without watching the Worktrees page. Limits are opt-in retention policy, which belongs in config plus the existing cleanup engine rather than a new subsystem.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- New config surface `worktrees.cleanup.maxCount` and `worktrees.cleanup.maxTotalSizeGb` (0 or unset disables each limit; default is unset, so existing installs see no behavior change).\n- Hourly gateway cleanup, `openclaw worktrees gc`, and the Control UI \"Clean up now\" action now snapshot and remove the least recently active session- and Workboard-owned worktrees until count and total size fit the configured limits.\n- Existing protections hold: manual worktrees, live/foreign locks, live run leases, and recently active session owners are never limit-evicted, and every eviction keeps the 30-day restorable snapshot.\n- Settings -> Worktrees gains a \"Cleanup\" section with two stepper controls; edits debounce into one minimal `config.patch` fragment.\n- Docs: configuration reference gains a Worktrees section; managed-worktrees concept doc documents the limit rules.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test src/agents/worktrees/service.test.ts src/gateway/server-maintenance.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/worktrees.test.ts src/config/config.schema-regressions.test.ts` on Blacksmith Testbox: 3 shards green (37 service tests incl. new count/size/eviction-order/protection coverage; schema regressions accept the new keys and reject negatives).\n- `pnpm test ui/src/pages/worktrees/worktrees-page.test.ts` on Blacksmith Testbox: green (renders values from config snapshot, disabled-until-loaded, debounced minimal patch, clamping + patch-failure surfacing).\n- Eviction policy unit-proven: oldest `lastActiveAt` first, manual worktrees counted but never evicted, active owners and locks skipped, limits ignored when unset.\n- `pnpm check:changed` on Blacksmith Testbox: all lanes green (format, plugin-sdk baselines, typecheck core, typecheck core tests re-run after a test-only fix).\n- Authenticated `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` run; all locales clean (fallbacks=0); `pnpm ui:i18n:check` green.\n- Visual proof (mock-gateway dev harness, deterministic fixtures):\n\n![Settings -> Worktrees with Cleanup limits](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/worktree-cleanup-limits/settings-worktrees-cleanup.png)\n\nStepper interaction verified in the harness: clicking + optimistically bumps the value, the debounced commit sends one minimal RFC 7396 fragment, and the value re-syncs from the config snapshot after refresh.\n",
        "branch": "claude/worktree-settings-ui-feature-742c0a",
